:EditPopupWindow
#############################
#####  EditPopupWindow  #####
#############################

	The EditPopupWindow will be displayed when the right mouse button is pressed
	when the mouse cursor is over an "XuiTextArea" or "XuiTextLine" type of grid.
	The EditPopupWindow will be displayed so that the "copy" command is under the
	mouse cursor. Normally, the window is hidden when a command is selected. But,
	if the "Shift" key is help down, the window will remain dislayed so that you
	may repeat a command several times without having to make it display again.
	
	To hide the EditPopupWindow without doing any of the commands,
	right click anywhere within the window, or press the "Esc" key.
	
	An "XuiTextArea" type grid will display these commands:
	
	  Cut
	  Copy
	  Paste
	  Copy Line
	  Duplicate Line
	  Cut Line
	
	An "XuiTextLine" type grid will display these choices:
	
	  Cut
	  Copy
	  Paste
	  Copy Line
	  Cut Line
	
	The "Console" and "instant help" windows will display these choices:
	
	  Copy
	  Copy Line
	
:Erase,                          main menu > Edit
##############################################################
#####  Erase,                          main menu > Edit  #####
##############################################################

	Delete selected text, but does not put a cop in the clipboard.
	
	This can also be done be pressing the "Delete" key.
	
:Erase Local Breakpoints,        main menu > Debug
###############################################################
#####  Erase Local Breakpoints,        main menu > Debug  #####
###############################################################

	Clear the breakpoint in the current function being edited
	
:Erase Output,                   main menu > Run
#############################################################
#####  Erase Output,                   main menu > Run  #####
#############################################################

	Clears the console screen
	
	See: XstClearConsole()
	
:Exit,                           main menu > File
##############################################################
#####  Exit,                           main menu > File  #####
##############################################################

	Close all windows and quit XBasic.
	
	If a user program is running, a warning message window
	will ask if it should stop program execution.
	
	If a user program has been modified and not save, a
	warning message will ask if the program should be saved.
	
	When XBasic exits normally, the filename, function and cursor position
	of the program being edited is saved in file .xbrc as well as the size
	and position of numerous windows. If there is an exception on exit,
	.xbrc is not written to ensure that it will not be curruped.
	
	
