:Help Index,                     main menu > Help
##############################################################
#####  Help Index,                     main menu > Help  #####
##############################################################

	Displays the Help Index, a list of all the XBasic
	functions, commands, messages etc. in alpabetical order.
	
	You can scroll down the list to the item of interest or
	type the item in the text line, the list will move as being
	typed to match.
	
	If there is selected text at the time the Help Index
	window is displayed, it will go to the matching location.
	
	The help information for any item can be displayed by
	double clicking on that item or, if the item of interest
	is highlighted, pressing the enter.
	
:Help Index Find,                main menu > Help
##############################################################
#####  Help Index Find,                main menu > Help  #####
##############################################################

	Displays the Help Index, a list of all the XBasic
	functions, commands, messages etc. in alpabetical order.
	
	Typing text in the text line will reduce the size of the list
	to only items of the index that contain a matching string.
	
	The help information for any item can be displayed by
	double clicking on that item or, if the item of interest
	is highlighted, pressing the enter.
	
:Jump,                           main menu > Run
#############################################################
#####  Jump,                           main menu > Run  #####
#############################################################

	The program must be the paused status for this to work.
	Make the active cursor line the line that has the instruction
	you wish to execute next.
	Then select Run > Jump
	The ">" should appear at the beginning of that line.
	Then, when you do a single-step or continue, execution
	will begin at that point.
	
	Stop user program execution
	
