########################################################################

	The following is a list of options from the
	"Miscellaneoous Options" window.
	They may be toggled on or off with mouse button.
	
	auto indent           - Enter key will add a new line with leading tabs
	                        and spaces the same as the previous line.
	auto upper case       - words that are entirley lower case and
	                        match keywords will be made upper case.
	check bounds          - checks that indexes to arrays are within limits
	                        and data access is of matching type.
	console dark color    - change the background color of the console to black.
	                        See: XstSetConsoleStyleAndColors()
	console large bars    - change the scrollbars on the console screen large.
	                        See: XstSetConsoleStyleAndColors()
	console large font    - change to a large character size on the console.
	                        See: XstSetConsoleFont()
	make backup file      - make a backup of the old version of a program
	                        before saving the new version.
	                        See: XBASICBACKUPDIR
	program large bars    - change the scrollbars on the edit program text screen large.
	program large font    - change to a large character size for the edit program text.
	program line numbers  - show line numbers for edit program text.
	reload last file      - when XBasic is started, load the file that was being edited
	                        when XBasic last quit and go to the last edit location.
	save before comp.     - save the user program before compiling it.
	save before run       - save the user program before running the program.
	save with \r\n        - when saving the user program, each text line is terminated with
	                        a carriage-return character and a line-feed character.
	stop compile on error - stop compiling a program at the end of a function if there is an error.
	tab block indent      - insert a tab at the begining of every line of the selected text,
	                        or remove a tab of every selected line for shift+tab
	
